Same ladder, same floor, same rungs, same depth schedule -> BYTE-IDENTICAL census readings.
Measured cost differs by the ratio above, entirely from `max_pool`. The census cannot see it.

====================================================================================================
C4 -- the mechanism: does cost track b1, or does the pool bind?
====================================================================================================

If round 1 floods the pool (b1 >> pool), round 2 composes over a POOL-SIZED census, so
cost ~ b1 + g(pool, library) -- additive in b1, not multiplicative. Test: cost/b1 should
COLLAPSE for rows where b1/pool is large, and the residual (cost - b1) should cluster by pool.

